732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7137   * all the most energy efficient CPU candidates (according to the Energy
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7138   * Model) are those for which we'll request a low frequency. When there are
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7139   * several CPUs for which the frequency request will be the same, we don't
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7140   * have enough data to break the tie between them, because the Energy Model
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7141   * only includes active power costs. With this model, if we assume that
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7142   * frequency requests follow utilization (e.g. using schedutil), the CPU with
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7143   * the maximum spare capacity in a performance domain is guaranteed to be among
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7144   * the best candidates of the performance domain.
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7145   *
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7146   * In practice, it could be preferable from an energy standpoint to pack
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7147   * small tasks on a CPU in order to let other CPUs go in deeper idle states,
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7148   * but that could also hurt our chances to go cluster idle, and we have no
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7149   * ways to tell with the current Energy Model if this is actually a good
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7150   * idea or not. So, find_energy_efficient_cpu() basically favors
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7151   * cluster-packing, and spreading inside a cluster. That should at least be
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7152   * a good thing for latency, and this is consistent with the idea that most
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7153   * of the energy savings of EAS come from the asymmetry of the system, and
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7154   * not so much from breaking the tie between identical CPUs. That's also the
732cd75b8c920d Quentin Perret            2018-12-03  7155   * reason why EAS is enabled in the topology code only for systems where
